.Dd March 19, 2026
.Dt TRUE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm true
.Nd return true value
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility always returns with a zero exit code.
.Pp
It may be shadowed by a shell built-in named
.Nm true
or by the special built-in
.Nm \&: .
This manual page documents the external utility.
.Pp
By default, this implementation adheres to BSD-priority semantics and ignores GNU long options such as
.Fl -help
and
.Fl -version ,
remaining silent and exiting successfully.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 unconditionally, indicating success.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr false 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is expected to be IEEE Std 1003.1-2024 ("POSIX.1") compatible.
